 "floorplan_note": "KV-AHUB5 10-19 variant A: Z inputs toward the centre, one inner strip per Z tree, z entries W/E at mid height. Children: u_zh0 MX at 43.2,43.2, u_zh1 R180 at 518.4,43.2, u_zh2 R0 at 43.2,345.6, u_zh3 MY at 518.4,345.6, u_recip R0 at 259.2,172.8. Clock entries: ck_c N 356-358 (core N pins x 216..443 above the core box), ck_w W 350-352, ck_e E 304-306, ck_z0 left 130-132, ck_z1 right 130-132, ck_z2 left 408-410, ck_z3 right 408-410. Region fences (lp_fences.tcl): c [194.4, 388.8, 518.4, 537.84]; w [2.16, 186.0, 43.2, 354.0]; e [680.4, 186.0, 732.24, 310.0]; z0 [43.2, 194.4, 194.4, 237.6]; z1 [518.4, 194.4, 669.6, 237.6]; z2 [43.2, 302.4, 194.4, 345.6]; z3 [518.4, 302.4, 669.6, 345.6]",
 "structural_change": "NEW kit (KV-AHUB5 10-19, after qkd_ahub_g3a / g3b gates FAIL clock_rule, ck_c 153.9-155.0 TT and Z roots 81.7-216.8 TT): same RTL as g3; the g3a per-flop census put ck_c's tail on the N-face pin flops 240 um above the core band (band 474..526 ps, pins 549..598) and each Z root's on reset pads in a second fence strip plus a trunk repaired after balancing.  (1) the core region is ONE box under its own N pins with the reciprocal leaf directly below; (2) one fence strip per Z tree (reset pads inside); (3) z clock entries midway between the strip and the macro clock pin (W/E faces); right-column Z trees mirrored so their clock pins face E.",
 "cycle_cost": "none vs g3 (same RTL and schedule): HUB_RECIP / HUB_PUB +6, am +3 at the ASTK pins, AP_OFS / FR_OFS / fr edge unchanged, reset release +10 once (results/arch/kv_ahub4_1019/README.md).",
